BUG-002: Missing Rate Limiting on Authentication / API Endpoint Allows Repeated Automated Requests
Severity: High | Priority: Medium
Module: Authentication & API Security
Environment: REST API (Tested via Postman)

Description:
Submitting repeated invalid requests to the login/verification endpoint does not trigger throttling or rate-limiting controls, allowing unrestricted automated attempts.

Steps to Reproduce:
1. Open Postman and configure a POST request to /api/auth/login with an invalid password payload.
2. Run 50 consecutive requests within 10 seconds using Postman Collection Runner.
3. Inspect HTTP status codes and response headers.

Expected Result:
- After a defined threshold of failed attempts, the API should return 429 Too Many Requests with a Retry-After header.

Actual Result:
- All 50 requests return 401 Unauthorized with no rate-limit headers or throttling enforced.
